Logger.razor (interactive, no prerendering):

```razor
<p>Hi</p>

@code {
    protected override void OnAfterRender(bool firstRender)
        => Console.WriteLine($"after {firstRender}");

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
        => Console.WriteLine("params");

    protected override void OnInitialized()
        => Console.WriteLine("init");
}
```

The component is shown once, and nothing else happens.

**What does the console show?**

Products.razor (interactive):

```razor
@page "/products"
@inject ProductService Service

<p>@products.Count products</p>

@code {
    private List<Product>? products;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        products = await Service.GetAllAsync(); // takes 1 second
    }
}
```

**What happens when you open the page?**

Stats.razor:

```razor
@page "/stats"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inject ILogger<Stats> Log

<p>Stats</p>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized()
        => Log.LogInformation("Loading stats");
}
```

Prerendering is on (the default). You open `/stats` once.

**How many times is "Loading stats" logged?**

Clock.razor (interactive):

```razor
<p>Seconds: @seconds</p>

@code {
    private int seconds;
    private Timer? timer;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        timer = new Timer(_ => seconds++, null, 1000, 1000);
    }
}
```

(`Timer` is `System.Threading.Timer`.) You wait 5 seconds and nothing else happens on the page.

**What does it show?**

